name w1-03-bvr-single-1
timeout 600

# CAMPAIGN W1, SORTIE 3 OF 10 - THE BVR INTERCEPT, ONE AGAINST ONE, RUNG 3 OF THE LADDER.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w1-red-flag.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: this file IS the control of w1-04-bvr-pair.fbm (the same lane, the same entry, the same racks,
# one more aircraft a side), and it is the SECOND geometry the saturation gate's doctrine sweep is flown
# on (doc/doctrine-evolution.md section 4.2, S2).
#
# THE ARENA is w1-01's lane at its FULL LENGTH: -115.52 to -116.58 at 37.30 N = 93.9 km, `--elev const`,
# 0 m range floor. The anchor and the substitution's direction are in w1-01-merge.fbm.
#
# THE ONE DEGREE OF FREEDOM this rung adds over rung 2: the RANGE AXIS. Rung 1 fought at 8 km, rung 2
# entered at 40 km, this one enters at 93.9 km with the full air-superiority racks - and the aircraft
# count goes back to one a side so that the range is the only thing that moved.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: at what multiple of Rtr does this pilot fire, and does the answer move when
# the opponent is the one carrying the longer Raero?
#
# WHAT THE ARENA ITSELF DOES TO THAT QUESTION, and it is the reason the lane's length is in every header:
# 93.9 km is SHORTER than the APG-68's own gate against this target (100.0 km), so Blue does not fly a
# search phase at all - it is handed the contact within seconds of the spawn. The N019's gate against an
# F-16 is 50.0 km, so the aggressor's first look comes at about 47 % of the way in. THE DETECTION
# ASYMMETRY OF THIS CAMPAIGN IS THEREFORE A PROPERTY OF THE RANGE'S SIZE and not of a mission setting;
# doc/duels.md row 1 measured the same pair over 111 km of open water, where Blue's search phase lasted
# 24.0 s. A Red Flag lane cannot be that long.
#
# THE LOADOUT IS DECLARED IN FIRING ORDER, which is doc/duels.md D4 and not a pylon map: weapon selection
# is not a decision either pilot can make (`FBCommandTarget::WeaponSelect` is NotImplemented on both
# modules), so the SMS steps through the occupied stations in ascending order and a mission that wants the
# radar rounds fired first has to put them on the low stations.
#
# THE GROUND: `nvhas3`, a bunkered defensive position [T1 target kind] at -116.20, i.e. BEHIND the merge
# from Blue's side, which is where the spec's rung 3 puts it. Campaign rule 3; not attacked (one `set
# task` per sortie).
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, campaign step 3 AND standalone - fingerprint 74c5812afdbd87e7, identical):
# exit 0. THE TRIGGER IS Rtr MINUS ONE DECISION TICK ON BOTH SIDES, AND IT DOES NOT MOVE.
#   Blue         shot t = 128.7 s at **9.570 nm** with Rtr **9.783** and Raero 31.09 -> **0.978 x Rtr**
#   the aggressor shot t = 127.3 s at **10.016 nm** with Rtr **10.254** and Raero 39.18 -> **0.977 x Rtr**
#   These are doc/duels.md row 1's published numbers (9.57/9.78 and 10.02/10.25, Raero 31.1/39.2) to two
#   decimal places, on a different arena, 8 degrees of latitude away, with four AIM-120 instead of two. SO
#   THE ANSWER TO THE SECOND HALF OF THE QUESTION IS NO: the opponent's Raero is a factor of **1.26**
#   longer and the two shot-to-Rtr ratios differ by **0.0015**. This pilot does not know what the other
#   jet's envelope is and the measurement says the trigger is blind to it.
#   detection    Blue at t = 3.9 s / **49.35 nm**, the aggressor at t = 78.1 s / 25.66 nm. duels.md row 1
#                measured 24.0 s / 52.19 nm for the same radar - THE 20 SECONDS ARE THE RANGE'S LENGTH
#                and not the sensor: 93.9 km of lane against a 100.0 km gate leaves no search phase
#   warning      Blue `eng_threat_s` 117.9 s, answered in 1.3 s. THE AGGRESSOR'S IS **-1**: it never knew
#                it was being worked, because the SPO-15 blanks +-90 deg forward while the N019 radiates
#                (doc/duels.md Knowledge 2) - reproduced here for the third time in the tree
#   arrivals     the first AIM-120 at **6.565 m** - no kill. The R-27R **EXPIRED** at 90.1 s of flight
#                with a closest approach of **16.35 m**. Then Blue re-merges, shoots again at t = 514.2 s
#                from 5,854 m and arrives at **1.179 m**: `damage KILL` at t = 520.6 s
# THE DRAW OF duels.md ROW 1 WAS A MAGAZINE, AND THIS IS THE THIRD ARENA THAT SAYS SO (O4-01 was the
# first). The sensor and trigger half reproduces to the second decimal; the outcome half is decided by how
# many rounds are left when the two jets meet again.
#
# WHAT TO READ: `eng_detect_s` / `eng_lock_s` / `eng_shot_s` / `eng_shot_nm` / `eng_shot_rtr_nm` per side
# - the shot's multiple of Rtr is `eng_shot_nm / eng_shot_rtr_nm` and both columns are published, so it is
# read and never recomputed - then `eng_support_f` / `eng_pitbull` (the R-27R runs to impact, the AIM-120
# does not: 17.3 s of binding against 0.3 s, doc/formation.md) and every `stores DETONATION missM` beside
# its own `fuzeM`.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is the expected shape of a two-sided intercept in which both jets
# declare `kill unit` + `survive`; the verdict is the `eng_*` block and the arrival geometry. READ THE
# DETECTION AND TRIGGER TIMES, NOT THE KILLS: O2 measured two R-27R inside their own fuze radius that did
# not kill and one further out that did, so an axis ordered by kills is reading warhead geometry. exit 2
# would be a defect.

unit rf3blu
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 37.30000 -115.52000 8000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink off                            # one against one: fought on own sensors
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -116.58000 8000 450
  objective kill unit rf3agr
  objective survive

unit rf3agr
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 37.30000 -116.58000 8000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set kols_mode ir
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 37.30000 -115.52000 8000 450
  objective kill unit rf3blu
  objective survive

unit nvhas3
  module target_hard                          # bunkered defensive position [T1 target kind]
  team hostile
  spawn 37.30000 -116.20000 ground 90.0 0
